238
00:08:06,333 --> 00:08:07,800
<b>That gap, between the</b>

239
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,133
<b>cost of grabbing someone</b>

240
00:08:09,266 --> 00:08:11,733
<b>and the price Europeans paid for them, is</b>

241
00:08:11,733 --> 00:08:13,833
<b>what made raiding economically rational.</b>

242
00:08:14,566 --> 00:08:16,800
<b>European demand created the gap.</b>

243
00:08:17,333 --> 00:08:18,233
<b>The Atlantic system</b>

244
00:08:18,233 --> 00:08:19,866
<b>didn't tap into a market.</b>

245
00:08:20,266 --> 00:08:22,433
<b>It created the incentive to build one.</b>

246
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:25,233
<b>Which brings us to the fourth document,</b>

247
00:08:25,466 --> 00:08:26,533
<b>the one that licensed</b>

248
00:08:26,533 --> 00:08:28,100
<b>this before it even scaled.</b>

249
00:08:28,899 --> 00:08:32,833
<b>On January 8th, 1455, Pope Nicholas V,</b>

250
00:08:33,433 --> 00:08:34,600
<b>the highest legal and</b>

251
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,100
<b>moral authority in Europe,</b>

252
00:08:36,533 --> 00:08:37,666
<b>issued a papal bull</b>

253
00:08:37,666 --> 00:08:39,833
<b>called "Romanus Pontifex",</b>

254
00:08:40,133 --> 00:08:41,566
<b>granting Portugal an</b>

255
00:08:41,566 --> 00:08:43,366
<b>exclusive monopoly in Africa.</b>

256
00:08:43,666 --> 00:08:45,333
<b>And this wasn't the first time.</b>

257
00:08:45,666 --> 00:08:48,333
<b>Three years earlier, in June 1452,</b>

258
00:08:48,833 --> 00:08:50,233
<b>Nicholas V had already</b>

259
00:08:50,233 --> 00:08:51,633
<b>signed "Dum Diversas".</b>

260
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:54,566
<b>"Romanus Pontifex" was the upgrade,</b>

261
00:08:54,766 --> 00:08:55,533
<b>giving Portugal</b>

262
00:08:55,533 --> 00:08:57,300
<b>exclusive rights across Africa.</b>

263
00:08:57,833 --> 00:09:00,699
<b>The bull authorizes Portugal to invade,</b>

264
00:09:00,766 --> 00:09:02,500
<b>search out and capture,</b>

265
00:09:02,733 --> 00:09:05,000
<b>to vanquish and subdue all</b>

266
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,699
<b>Saracens and Pagans whatsoever,</b>

267
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:08,933
<b>and to reduce their</b>

268
00:09:08,933 --> 00:09:11,199
<b>persons to perpetual slavery.</b>

269
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,433
<b>This was 1455.</b>

270
00:09:14,233 --> 00:09:16,399
<b>The legal authority for perpetual slavery</b>

271
00:09:16,399 --> 00:09:19,066
<b>was drawn up before the commerce existed,</b>

272
00:09:19,833 --> 00:09:21,666
<b>and the operators relied on it.</b>

273
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,366
<b>Prince Henry himself cited</b>

274
00:09:24,366 --> 00:09:26,800
<b>various earlier papal bulls</b>

275
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:27,833
<b>as the powerful</b>

276
00:09:27,833 --> 00:09:29,566
<b>authority for his slave trade.</b>

277
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:32,233
<b>The Pope didn't license a market.</b>

278
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,133
<b>He licensed a conquest.</b>

279
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,866
<b>In August 1518, the King of Spain issued</b>

280
00:09:37,866 --> 00:09:39,766
<b>the license to Lorenzo de Gorrevod.</b>

281
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:40,866
<b>The terms?</b>

282
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:43,566
<b>Gorrevod is authorized to transport</b>

283
00:09:43,566 --> 00:09:45,133
<b>4,000 African slaves,</b>

284
00:09:45,366 --> 00:09:46,800
<b>male and female, to the</b>

285
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,699
<b>Spanish colonies in the New World.</b>

286
00:09:49,166 --> 00:09:50,433
<b>They must be Christians.</b>

287
00:09:50,666 --> 00:09:54,433
<b>They should bypass Seville, 4,000 people</b>

288
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:56,033
<b>in a single contract.</b>

289
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,666
<b>The "provided they be</b>

290
00:09:57,666 --> 00:10:00,500
<b>Christians" clause was the legal alibi.</b>

291
00:10:01,033 --> 00:10:03,266
<b>Captives were baptized on arrival,</b>

292
00:10:03,533 --> 00:10:06,500
<b>reframing kidnapping as salvation.</b>

293
00:10:06,833 --> 00:10:07,766
<b>This is the asiento.</b>

294
00:10:08,366 --> 00:10:10,566
<b>The moment the papal license became a</b>

295
00:10:10,566 --> 00:10:12,066
<b>commercial contract,</b>

296
00:10:12,566 --> 00:10:13,800
<b>the bull authorized</b>

297
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:16,133
<b>perpetual slavery in 1455.</b>

298
00:10:16,833 --> 00:10:19,266
<b>By 1518, the Spanish crown was</b>

299
00:10:19,266 --> 00:10:21,533
<b>contracting for it by the 1,000.</b>

300
00:10:22,166 --> 00:10:24,033
<b>The Pope didn't just bless a market.</b>

301
00:10:24,366 --> 00:10:26,100
<b>He chartered an industry.</b>

302
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:28,566
<b>Five documents, the</b>

303
00:10:28,566 --> 00:10:30,133
<b>Chronicle of the First Raids,</b>

304
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:32,033
<b>the Desperate Letter of an African King,</b>

305
00:10:32,566 --> 00:10:34,666
<b>the frustration of a European buyer,</b>

306
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,699
<b>the legal decree of the Pope,</b>

307
00:10:37,033 --> 00:10:38,133
<b>and the royal license</b>

308
00:10:38,133 --> 00:10:39,699
<b>that put it into practice.</b>

309
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:42,333
<b>I'm not under any illusion this will</b>

310
00:10:42,333 --> 00:10:44,066
<b>convince people who use history</b>

311
00:10:44,066 --> 00:10:45,500
<b>as a weapon in a culture war.</b>

312
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:48,433
<b>But for everyone else, what these five</b>

313
00:10:48,433 --> 00:10:50,000
<b>documents show is this.</b>

314
00:10:50,666 --> 00:10:52,166
<b>The talking point is too</b>

315
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:53,866
<b>broad to show the full picture.</b>

316
00:10:54,333 --> 00:10:56,300
<b>Yes, slavery existed</b>

317
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:57,833
<b>before Europeans arrived.</b>

318
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:00,699
<b>But what didn't exist was the scale,</b>

319
00:11:01,166 --> 00:11:03,933
<b>the legal authority, and the racial logic</b>

320
00:11:03,933 --> 00:11:05,133
<b>that made it permanent.</b>

